---
title: Design class diagram 7 of 8 - authentication services (Strategies.Api/Services)
---
classDiagram
    direction LR

    class AuthService {
        <<service, scoped>>
        -_dbContext: ApplicationDbContext
        -_passwordHasher: IPasswordHasherService
        -_tokenService: ITokenService
        -_refreshTokenStore: IRefreshTokenStore
        -_logger: ILogger~AuthService~
        -_lazySeedUsers: Lazy~List~User~~$
        -_dbConnectionChecked: bool = false
        -_dbAvailable: bool = false
        +LoginAsync(request: LoginRequest) Task~AuthResponse?~
        +RefreshTokenAsync(refreshTokenString: string) Task~AuthResponse?~
        +RevokeTokenAsync(refreshTokenString: string) Task~bool~
        +GetUserByIdAsync(userId: Guid) Task~User?~
        +GetUserByEmailAsync(email: string) Task~User?~
        +RegisterAsync(request: RegisterRequest) Task~bool~
        +ResetPasswordAsync(request: ResetPasswordRequest) Task~bool~
        -IsDbAvailableAsync() Task~bool~
    }
    class TokenService {
        <<service, singleton>>
        -_config: IConfiguration
        -_key: SymmetricSecurityKey
        -_issuer: string
        -_audience: string
        -_accessTokenExpirationMinutes: int
        -_refreshTokenExpirationDays: int
        +AccessTokenExpirationMinutes: int «get»
        +RefreshTokenExpirationDays: int «get»
        +GenerateAccessToken(user: User) ValueTuple~string, DateTime~
        +GenerateRefreshToken() string
    }
    class PasswordHasherService {
        <<service, singleton>>
        +HashPassword(password: string) string
        +VerifyPassword(password: string, hashedPassword: string) bool
    }
    class InMemoryRefreshTokenStore {
        <<service, singleton>>
        -_tokens: ConcurrentDictionary~string, RefreshToken~
        -EvictionGracePeriod: TimeSpan = 24 h$
        +SaveTokenAsync(token: RefreshToken) Task
        +GetTokenAsync(token: string) Task~RefreshToken?~
        +RevokeTokenAsync(token: string, replacedByToken: string? = null) Task
        +RevokeAllUserTokensAsync(userId: Guid) Task
        -EvictStaleTokens() void
    }
    class RefreshToken {
        +Token: string
        +UserId: Guid
        +CreatedAt: DateTime = UtcNow
        +ExpiresAt: DateTime
        +IsRevoked: bool
        +RevokedAt: DateTime?
        +ReplacedByToken: string?
        +IsExpired: bool «get, derived»
        +IsActive: bool «get, derived»
    }

    AuthService --() IAuthService
    TokenService --() ITokenService
    PasswordHasherService --() IPasswordHasherService
    InMemoryRefreshTokenStore --() IRefreshTokenStore
    InMemoryRefreshTokenStore "1" o-- "0..*" RefreshToken

    note "Lollipop = interface the class provides. Each interface declares<br>exactly the public operations listed in its class (IAuthService,<br>ITokenService, IPasswordHasherService, IRefreshTokenStore).<br>AuthService uses the other three through its private fields<br>(constructor injection). Lifetimes are from Program.cs.<br>GenerateAccessToken returns the named tuple (Token, Expiration).<br>PasswordHasherService: BCrypt, work factor 11.<br>Refresh tokens live in memory and are lost on restart.<br>If the database is unreachable, AuthService reads the<br>in-code _lazySeedUsers list instead (IsDbAvailableAsync)."
